"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nHe lived faithfully supporting his family as the head of the household, but as soon as he turns into a monster, the family members gradually reject and loathe him.  \nAs time passes, he remains locked in his room, gradually weakening, and faces a death that no one grieves.  \nThe family prepares for a new beginning with relief as soon as he dies.  \n\nIt depicts the deletion of existence experienced by a human when they lose social function.  \nAlthough it was published over a century ago, the theme contained in this work still deeply resonates in modern society.  \n\n\n"